WEBVTT

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.174
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

00:00:06.424 --> 00:00:09.010
(Get ready, dig your anger up, MOB!)

00:00:09.260 --> 00:00:11.888
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

00:00:12.138 --> 00:00:13.389
(Get ready!)

00:00:14.182 --> 00:00:18.645
Coming down,
could you fill your satisfaction?

00:00:19.854 --> 00:00:24.150
You're a MOB.
Can't you feel your own frustration?

00:00:25.527 --> 00:00:29.906
Coming down,
could you fill your satisfaction?

00:00:31.241 --> 00:00:34.035
You're a MOB.
What do you want to be?

00:00:34.285 --> 00:00:41.000
Wear your overflowing emotions
on your sleeve and break it down

00:00:42.835 --> 00:00:46.130
What do you see once you go
beyond your limits?

00:00:46.381 --> 00:00:49.050
(99.9! 99.9)

00:00:49.300 --> 00:00:52.220
The mysterious percentage

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:56.391
Cr yin' my life, or yin' my psyche,

00:00:56.641 --> 00:00:59.394
Cr yin' my heart in such commonplaces!

00:00:59.644 --> 00:01:02.230
Is that your ideal? Is that your mind?

00:01:02.480 --> 00:01:05.066
It all begins when it hits 100

00:01:05.316 --> 00:01:07.902
The MOB is alive. The MOB is high.

00:01:08.152 --> 00:01:10.780
The MOB is staying frustrated, aren't you?

00:01:11.030 --> 00:01:15.118
Is that your ideal?
Is that your mind? Right now

00:01:16.578 --> 00:01:17.704
YOUR LIFE IS YOUR OWN.

00:01:17.954 --> 00:01:20.290
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

00:01:20.290 --> 00:01:20.415
"Mob Psycho 100 II"
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

00:01:20.415 --> 00:01:20.665
"Mob Psycho 100 II"

00:01:20.665 --> 00:01:23.251
"Mob Psycho 100 II"
(Get ready, dig your anger up, MOB!)

00:01:23.251 --> 00:01:23.501
"Mob Psycho 100 II"

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:24.836
"Mob Psycho 100 II"
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

00:01:24.836 --> 00:01:26.170
(Get ready, wake your psyche up, MOB!)

00:01:26.421 --> 00:01:27.672
(Get ready!)

00:01:30.008 --> 00:01:33.928
"The Battle for Social Rehabilitation
- Friendship~"

00:01:34.596 --> 00:01:38.558
Leave. I don't want you to get hurt.

00:01:38.808 --> 00:01:40.977
You can take this guy back with you, too.

00:01:41.227 --> 00:01:42.770
He's supposed to be a hostage,

00:01:43.021 --> 00:01:44.272
but I feel bad for him.

00:01:44.522 --> 00:01:46.482
Oh, it's the prime minister guy.

00:01:46.733 --> 00:01:49.611
What? You're the prime minister?!

00:01:49.861 --> 00:01:51.738
I-I'm free to go?

00:01:51.988 --> 00:01:53.197
Go right ahead.

00:01:54.616 --> 00:01:57.994
Holy cow... I just talked
to the prime minister!

00:01:58.244 --> 00:02:01.247
You're part of the group that abducted him,
and you had no idea?

00:02:01.497 --> 00:02:03.583
Well, you know, I don't watch TV.

00:02:03.833 --> 00:02:08.004
I see. So the public thinks
we're the bad guys.

00:02:08.254 --> 00:02:11.841
But you are, though. Look at
how much damage you've done to the city.

00:02:12.091 --> 00:02:16.804
It's fine. The president said that
most people had already evacuated.

00:02:17.055 --> 00:02:17.889
President?

00:02:18.139 --> 00:02:20.266
The person who hired me.

00:02:20.516 --> 00:02:24.687
He rescued me from
the hellhole that was my life.

00:02:24.979 --> 00:02:25.813
"3 Years Ago"

00:02:26.064 --> 00:02:27.315
"Serizawa Katsuya"
"27 years old"

00:02:31.069 --> 00:02:34.947
It's filthy in here. Why have you
been a shut-in for 15 years?

00:02:35.948 --> 00:02:37.075
Who're you?

00:02:37.325 --> 00:02:39.327
My name is Suzuki.

00:02:39.577 --> 00:02:42.372
Your mother asked me to help you.

00:02:42.622 --> 00:02:44.582
Another counselor?

00:02:44.832 --> 00:02:48.544
Just know that if you get
any closer, you'll get hurt.

00:02:48.795 --> 00:02:50.380
I'm not normal.

00:02:50.630 --> 00:02:53.132
I hear that you're an esper.

00:02:53.383 --> 00:02:55.134
I understand how you feel.

00:02:55.385 --> 00:02:57.345
Yeah, no. Go away.

00:02:57.595 --> 00:03:02.141
Why? Why don't you tell me
how you're feeling?

00:03:02.392 --> 00:03:04.811
No... Don't say anything else.

00:03:05.061 --> 00:03:07.063
Please, I'm begging you. Don't annoy me.

00:03:07.313 --> 00:03:08.898
It must be hard...

00:03:09.148 --> 00:03:11.901
...not being able to make friends
because people find your powers creepy.

00:03:11.901 --> 00:03:12.068
"Potato Chips" ...not being able to make
friends because people find your powers creepy.

00:03:12.068 --> 00:03:12.318
"Potato Chips"

00:03:12.318 --> 00:03:14.070
"Potato Chips"
Stop. Don't act like you know how I feel.

00:03:14.070 --> 00:03:14.821
"Potato Chips" "Yeet Tea" Stop.
Don't act like you know how I feel.

00:03:14.821 --> 00:03:14.946
Stop. Don't act like you know how I feel.

00:03:15.196 --> 00:03:16.698
Go away! Just go away!

00:03:16.948 --> 00:03:20.702
You must've been bullied
out of your place in society.

00:03:23.287 --> 00:03:25.081
Get out!

00:03:28.042 --> 00:03:30.336
I'm an esper, too, you see.

00:03:30.586 --> 00:03:32.380
Come with me.

00:03:33.339 --> 00:03:37.176
B-But I get dizzy whenever I leave my room.

00:03:39.595 --> 00:03:41.639
It was raining outside.

00:03:41.889 --> 00:03:44.183
This umbrella is for you.

00:03:44.434 --> 00:03:47.979
Just imagine that when you're under
this umbrella, you're in your room.

00:03:48.229 --> 00:03:52.150
Don't worry. You'll be fine if you're with me.

00:03:52.400 --> 00:03:54.986
I'll show you how to use your powers.

00:03:56.028 --> 00:03:59.282
After that, I became an
upper echelon employee of Claw

00:03:59.532 --> 00:04:01.701
and regained my place in society.

00:04:01.951 --> 00:04:03.286
That's weird.

00:04:03.536 --> 00:04:04.328
Huh?

00:04:04.579 --> 00:04:07.957
Even I can tell that's all kinds of wrong.

00:04:08.207 --> 00:04:11.169
Aren't you basically just being used?

00:04:12.170 --> 00:04:13.838
Look who's talking!

00:04:14.088 --> 00:04:17.091
What a horrible thing to say...

00:04:17.341 --> 00:04:19.051
You're the one who's horrible.

00:04:19.302 --> 00:04:23.347
If this is what you were going to do,
you should've just stayed a shut-in.

00:04:23.598 --> 00:04:26.517
Can't you picture the faces of
the people impacted by this?

00:04:26.768 --> 00:04:31.731
The president said that world domination
always involved certain sacrifices.

00:04:31.981 --> 00:04:33.983
Do you believe that, too?

00:04:34.233 --> 00:04:37.820
Hey... could you leave?

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:42.116
Serizawa-san, you chose
the wrong person to follow.

00:04:48.080 --> 00:04:49.081
You okay?

00:04:49.332 --> 00:04:50.249
That umbrella...

00:04:50.500 --> 00:04:53.628
Yeah, it's shrouded in some insane power.

00:04:53.878 --> 00:04:57.799
I can relax when I'm under this umbrella.

00:04:58.049 --> 00:04:59.759
If we can take his umbrella...

00:05:00.009 --> 00:05:01.761
He'll lose his strength.

00:05:14.649 --> 00:05:17.693
Trying to immobilize me...
isn't going to work!

00:05:17.944 --> 00:05:19.529
Ow...

00:05:19.779 --> 00:05:22.698
Oh, sorry. Are you okay?

00:05:22.949 --> 00:05:24.575
Wait, you were faking?

00:05:24.826 --> 00:05:25.660
Now, Dimple!

00:05:25.910 --> 00:05:27.119
You got it!

00:05:30.790 --> 00:05:32.208
Oh, shit!

00:05:34.669 --> 00:05:37.839
He explodes after only a second
without his umbrella?

00:05:38.089 --> 00:05:40.591
He must be incredibly anxious.

00:05:40.842 --> 00:05:42.635
He finally found someone
who understood him.

00:05:42.885 --> 00:05:44.387
He had no choice but to follow him.

00:05:45.346 --> 00:05:49.976
He never stood a chance against someone
who used that to their advantage.

00:05:50.226 --> 00:05:51.894
I have to tell him.

00:05:52.144 --> 00:05:55.648
That president of yours
didn't give you peace.

00:05:55.898 --> 00:05:58.609
He gave you the idea that
you can't live on your own

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:00.903
and chained you to the organization.

00:06:02.154 --> 00:06:03.865
Are you a counselor?

00:06:04.115 --> 00:06:05.992
You can't reintegrate into society this way.

00:06:06.242 --> 00:06:09.954
If anything, at this rate,
you'll never be able to return.

00:06:10.204 --> 00:06:13.624
Like a kid who still has his whole future
ahead of him knows how I feel.

00:06:13.875 --> 00:06:17.503
Then tell me... What the hell
am I supposed to do?!

00:06:17.753 --> 00:06:20.548
No one understood this power
I was born with!

00:06:20.798 --> 00:06:23.843
People thought I was creepy,
so I'd lose control and cause people trouble!

00:06:24.093 --> 00:06:26.679
And because of that,
I'd get scorned and lose control again!

00:06:26.929 --> 00:06:29.098
I even accidentally sent
my mother flying before!

00:06:29.348 --> 00:06:32.935
I never had any idea
when I might lose control!

00:06:33.185 --> 00:06:36.480
I couldn't even talk to anyone...

00:06:36.731 --> 00:06:39.066
I just...

00:06:39.317 --> 00:06:42.028
I dunno... I just wanted...

00:06:43.029 --> 00:06:46.365
I just wanted friends.

00:06:49.285 --> 00:06:51.537
I have friends here.

00:06:51.787 --> 00:06:53.789
Espers just like me!

00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:55.625
You'd never understand!

00:06:59.670 --> 00:07:02.590
Of course I understand.
They aren't your friends.

00:07:03.841 --> 00:07:06.052
I actually have friends.

00:07:06.302 --> 00:07:07.678
That's how I know.

00:07:07.929 --> 00:07:09.764
They aren't your friends.

00:07:10.014 --> 00:07:13.309
Stop... Stop saying that over and over!

00:07:14.518 --> 00:07:17.271
This isn't good, Shigeo!
That's an insane amount of energy!

00:07:17.521 --> 00:07:20.524
I won't let you go any further!
Those are the president's orders!

00:07:20.775 --> 00:07:23.069
The president trusts me!

00:07:23.319 --> 00:07:25.988
No, it has nothing to do with trust.

00:07:27.657 --> 00:07:29.617
You're just being used.

00:07:29.867 --> 00:07:33.412
No! The president gave me a reason to live!

00:07:33.663 --> 00:07:36.082
But he doesn't see you as a person!

00:07:37.083 --> 00:07:39.210
As a person?

00:07:39.460 --> 00:07:42.171
You said you didn't want to hurt anyone.

00:07:42.421 --> 00:07:43.839
You're just like me.

00:07:44.090 --> 00:07:45.758
I know you realize

00:07:46.008 --> 00:07:47.969
that you're wrong.

00:07:48.219 --> 00:07:50.012
Shut up!

00:07:51.180 --> 00:07:54.976
In that case... I'll be your friend.

00:07:55.226 --> 00:07:56.060
Huh?

00:07:56.310 --> 00:07:57.353
Whoops...

00:07:58.020 --> 00:07:59.313
I shot at him.

00:08:01.607 --> 00:08:03.401
Shigeo!

00:08:03.651 --> 00:08:05.069
I even went all out!

00:08:10.741 --> 00:08:11.993
What?!

00:08:14.537 --> 00:08:17.665
You're sucking up my energy?

00:08:17.915 --> 00:08:20.459
I can sense what you're feeling.

00:08:20.710 --> 00:08:23.295
Such a sad energy...

00:08:23.546 --> 00:08:26.007
You turned it into your own power?

00:08:26.257 --> 00:08:29.093
No. You can have it back, Serizawa-san.

00:08:35.975 --> 00:08:37.560
What is this?

00:08:39.353 --> 00:08:40.646
I see...

00:08:40.896 --> 00:08:42.481
He's...

00:08:42.732 --> 00:08:44.358
He's the same as me...

00:08:45.651 --> 00:08:47.820
"Friendship"

00:08:49.238 --> 00:08:54.493
Now I'm going to have to recruit more
soldiers because of you and your friends.

00:08:54.744 --> 00:08:56.829
Stop this already, Dad.

00:08:57.079 --> 00:09:00.875
You can see that they aren't much help.

00:09:01.125 --> 00:09:04.628
Since you're my son,
I'll go ahead and tell you.

00:09:04.879 --> 00:09:07.173
The project of applying stress
to normal human beings

00:09:07.423 --> 00:09:10.009
to awaken any ESP they may have...

00:09:10.259 --> 00:09:12.011
It was a failure.

00:09:12.261 --> 00:09:14.180
Even if they did happen
to awaken to some powers,

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:17.850
the most they could do was produce
some insignificant phenomenon.

00:09:18.100 --> 00:09:20.144
Then their powers...

00:09:20.394 --> 00:09:22.563
You call that an insignificant phenomenon?

00:09:23.606 --> 00:09:26.692
The powers they're using
like they're going out of fashion

00:09:26.942 --> 00:09:29.153
are my powers.

00:09:29.403 --> 00:09:32.615
I am able to share my power with others.

00:09:32.865 --> 00:09:36.577
At the same time, I am able to absorb
other people's powers as my own.

00:09:36.827 --> 00:09:41.373
This is my true trump card
that no one knew about.

00:09:41.624 --> 00:09:45.086
So you gave 600 soldiers your power?

00:09:45.336 --> 00:09:50.341
That's just a mere fraction of
the energy that I have accumulated.

00:09:50.591 --> 00:09:53.761
But that doesn't make it any less vital.

00:09:54.011 --> 00:09:57.098
I'll be reclaiming my energy
from those who have lost.

00:10:09.860 --> 00:10:12.029
I-1 finally understand...

00:10:12.279 --> 00:10:14.281
My dad's not human.

00:10:14.532 --> 00:10:16.700
He's a monster made up of energy!

00:10:16.951 --> 00:10:19.203
Let this be a lesson, Sho.

00:10:19.453 --> 00:10:24.959
Only one absolute being can be
the true protagonist of this world.

00:10:25.209 --> 00:10:26.710
Absolute being?

00:10:30.256 --> 00:10:31.423
You're--

00:10:40.266 --> 00:10:41.892
You're Ritsu's older bro.

00:10:42.143 --> 00:10:46.522
That must mean my detonator
went off successfully.

00:10:46.772 --> 00:10:50.442
Are you the one who set fire to my house?

00:10:50.693 --> 00:10:54.155
You're probably pissed off about that,
but you should probably run.

00:10:54.405 --> 00:10:57.283
There's no one in this world
who can defeat him.

00:10:57.533 --> 00:11:01.328
I'm not mad anymore.
I'm sure you have a lot going on.

00:11:01.579 --> 00:11:04.498
I mean, look at what
your own father has done to you.

00:11:05.749 --> 00:11:07.126
Who are you?

00:11:07.376 --> 00:11:11.672
He's been worried about you
losing control. I can tell.

00:11:11.922 --> 00:11:15.092
Because my younger brother
was afraid of me, too.

00:11:15.342 --> 00:11:17.636
He's... changed.

00:11:17.887 --> 00:11:21.599
You make it sound like you know
what's going on with our family.

00:11:21.849 --> 00:11:26.729
Serizawa-san told me that
your son was trying to stop you.

00:11:26.979 --> 00:11:28.606
That your son was being beaten so badly,

00:11:28.856 --> 00:11:31.942
he couldn't bear to watch
and came downstairs...

00:11:32.193 --> 00:11:34.445
That he felt so pathetic
for not being able to step in,

00:11:34.695 --> 00:11:36.405
making him want to disappear.

00:11:36.655 --> 00:11:38.949
Serizawa lost?

00:11:39.200 --> 00:11:41.327
That moron. He must've gotten sloppy.

00:11:41.577 --> 00:11:42.536
You're wrong.

00:11:42.786 --> 00:11:44.163
Winning and losing

00:11:44.413 --> 00:11:47.333
isn't the be-all and end-all
in relationships between people.

00:11:48.918 --> 00:11:51.670
It was the president
who got me out of that room.

00:11:51.921 --> 00:11:53.339
I'm grateful to him.

00:11:53.589 --> 00:11:57.343
But why is there a need to hurt people?

00:11:57.593 --> 00:12:00.304
I've been too scared to think about it
so I've been running away...

00:12:00.554 --> 00:12:03.224
But if my happiness only came
as a result of another's tears,

00:12:03.474 --> 00:12:05.559
I never wanted it in the first place.

00:12:06.602 --> 00:12:09.188
Thank you for making me realize that.

00:12:11.523 --> 00:12:15.152
Apparently, trash will never be
anything more than trash.

00:12:15.402 --> 00:12:19.073
So be it. It's not like I ever truly
counted on others to begin with.

00:12:19.323 --> 00:12:22.368
Bonds with others are absolutely meaningless.

00:12:22.618 --> 00:12:26.080
After all, I am whole on my own.

00:12:26.330 --> 00:12:29.250
That's not true. Everyone...

00:12:29.500 --> 00:12:32.962
Everyone grows because of their
encounters with other people.

00:12:33.212 --> 00:12:35.381
People need other people.

00:12:35.631 --> 00:12:37.800
Someday, you'll need others.

00:12:38.050 --> 00:12:41.011
When that time comes,
you're surely going to regret things.

00:12:41.262 --> 00:12:44.390
So if you don't have anyone to talk to,

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:45.557
I'll be there.

00:12:45.808 --> 00:12:48.018
You want to be a shoulder I can lean on?

00:12:49.353 --> 00:12:52.398
Save that kind of talk
for the weaklings of the world.

00:12:52.648 --> 00:12:57.611
Ritsu's bro, he can give people his energy
and steal theirs in turn.

00:12:57.861 --> 00:13:00.990
On top of that, he's got
a massive stock of energy himself.

00:13:01.240 --> 00:13:04.952
Meanwhile, I can barely even move...

00:13:05.202 --> 00:13:06.829
Will this help you move?

00:13:07.079 --> 00:13:08.539
What?

00:13:08.789 --> 00:13:10.958
Th-This is...

00:13:12.334 --> 00:13:13.877
He has the same power as me?

00:13:14.128 --> 00:13:14.920
Can you move?

00:13:15.170 --> 00:13:17.923
Y-Yeah, I can sorta stand.

00:13:18.173 --> 00:13:20.843
That's good. In that case,
you should evacuate, too.

00:13:21.093 --> 00:13:22.219
I'm going to--

00:13:22.845 --> 00:13:24.888
I have acknowledged you as my enemy.

00:13:26.473 --> 00:13:27.433
Stop!

00:13:28.517 --> 00:13:29.935
You stay out of this.

00:13:30.185 --> 00:13:32.688
He has the potential to
become my mortal enemy.

00:13:32.938 --> 00:13:36.108
Don't. I came here to talk.

00:13:36.358 --> 00:13:37.818
Give it up, Shigeo!

00:13:38.068 --> 00:13:39.611
You can't talk to guys like--

00:13:40.696 --> 00:13:41.905
You're an annoyance.

00:13:42.156 --> 00:13:43.407
You can disappear first.

00:13:43.657 --> 00:13:44.616
Dimple!

00:13:48.245 --> 00:13:51.332
Was it really a good idea to
let Kageyama-kun go off alone?

00:13:51.582 --> 00:13:55.544
I've never seen my brother
openly stamp his authority like that.

00:13:55.794 --> 00:13:58.213
He looked in pain to me, though.

00:13:58.464 --> 00:14:01.425
He's not usually the type to fight.

00:14:01.675 --> 00:14:04.094
What do you think, Reigen-san?

00:14:04.345 --> 00:14:08.432
At first glance, Mob looks pretty unreliable,
but his strength is undeniable.

00:14:08.682 --> 00:14:11.060
His insane telekinesis, right?

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:15.397
That's just one of his qualities.

00:14:15.647 --> 00:14:17.733
What makes him truly great

00:14:17.983 --> 00:14:20.861
is his ability to tell people
exactly how he feels.

00:14:21.111 --> 00:14:24.239
And that speaks to their heart
far more than any niceties.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:28.077
As long as Mob's feelings can be
expressed to whoever he's facing...

00:14:32.206 --> 00:14:33.082
Dimple!

00:14:33.332 --> 00:14:34.708
What's wrong? Are you okay?

00:14:34.958 --> 00:14:36.126
Where's Mob?

00:14:36.377 --> 00:14:39.296
I'm not sure, but things look pretty grim.

00:14:39.546 --> 00:14:43.300
The enemy was pretty intent
on mercilessly killing Shigeo.

00:14:43.550 --> 00:14:45.302
Four-eyes, you got a sec?

00:14:48.055 --> 00:14:49.473
Talk?

00:14:49.723 --> 00:14:52.601
You said that bonds with others
are meaningless.

00:14:52.851 --> 00:14:54.520
That can't be true.

00:14:54.770 --> 00:14:55.646
Everyone lacks something.

00:14:55.896 --> 00:15:00.150
People making up for others' deficiencies
is what makes this world go around.

00:15:00.401 --> 00:15:03.070
All of you are so boring.

00:15:03.320 --> 00:15:07.324
Even among those
blessed with the gift of ESP,

00:15:07.574 --> 00:15:10.494
my powers far surpass them all.

00:15:10.744 --> 00:15:13.330
When I came to that realization,

00:15:13.580 --> 00:15:17.000
it appeared as though this world
could fit in the palm of my hand.

00:15:17.251 --> 00:15:20.921
That was when I was in middle school,
same as the two of you.

00:15:21.171 --> 00:15:25.384
But your mindset
puts a halt to all progress,

00:15:25.634 --> 00:15:30.305
leaving you living a boring life
just like the powerless.

00:15:30.556 --> 00:15:31.598
That's not true.

00:15:31.849 --> 00:15:35.644
You're the one who's stopped in place
since middle school.

00:15:35.894 --> 00:15:39.690
There are far more unique people
in this world than you think,

00:15:39.940 --> 00:15:42.025
and just as many mindsets.

00:15:42.276 --> 00:15:47.072
No one should be able to place a value
on another person's mindset.

00:15:47.322 --> 00:15:50.033
You sound like you're trying
to take the moral high ground.

00:15:50.284 --> 00:15:53.954
I have no need to rely on others
to make up for my deficiencies

00:15:54.204 --> 00:15:58.250
because I have the ability
to steal, use, and rule.

00:15:58.625 --> 00:15:59.668
"Claw"

00:15:59.668 --> 00:16:00.294
"Claw" My goal in life is to
leave a huge mark upon this world.

00:16:00.294 --> 00:16:06.008
My goal in life is to leave
a huge mark upon this world.

00:16:07.718 --> 00:16:09.219
Ritsu's bro,

00:16:09.470 --> 00:16:12.055
don't worry about me. Just finish him off!

00:16:12.306 --> 00:16:18.479
Sho, I'd thought about letting you inherit
the world I was going to take over,

00:16:18.729 --> 00:16:22.024
but apparently you've become a failure.

00:16:24.234 --> 00:16:25.277
Hey.

00:16:29.198 --> 00:16:31.533
Are you angry on Sho's behalf?

00:16:32.659 --> 00:16:34.411
You truly are a child.

00:16:34.661 --> 00:16:36.163
Be quiet.

00:16:36.413 --> 00:16:39.833
This is amusing, though.
Show me everything you've got.

00:16:42.711 --> 00:16:44.963
This is rough...

00:16:54.473 --> 00:16:56.683
Stop!

00:16:59.353 --> 00:17:00.854
Just sit there and watch.

00:17:01.104 --> 00:17:03.106
This is what happens to weaklings.

00:17:06.026 --> 00:17:10.489
Still, you sure have some nerve
to lecture me when you're so weak.

00:17:10.739 --> 00:17:12.533
You can't be serious.

00:17:12.783 --> 00:17:13.825
Don't move.

00:17:15.369 --> 00:17:17.120
It's loaded, by the way.

00:17:18.413 --> 00:17:20.666
Sakurai's Jugan.

00:17:20.916 --> 00:17:23.627
You can't threaten me
with something like that.

00:17:23.877 --> 00:17:26.338
M-Master...

00:17:26.588 --> 00:17:30.133
Hey, Mob.

00:17:30.384 --> 00:17:32.803
I don't sense any power from you.

00:17:33.053 --> 00:17:35.847
You'll stay out of this
if you know what's best for you.

00:17:39.476 --> 00:17:42.604
Apparently, you still don't
understand how powerful I am.

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:46.275
Hey, you alive, Mob?

00:17:47.568 --> 00:17:50.862
I don't know what I was thinking,
letting you go off alone like that.

00:17:51.113 --> 00:17:52.322
I think my ability to think

00:17:52.573 --> 00:17:54.658
was impacted by all
the unnatural things going on.

00:17:55.951 --> 00:17:57.995
I failed as a master.

00:17:58.245 --> 00:18:01.248
You did well. I'll treat you to
some takoyaki on our way home.

00:18:01.498 --> 00:18:02.708
Master?

00:18:02.958 --> 00:18:06.128
Even though you can't even see
how powerful I am?

00:18:06.378 --> 00:18:11.508
So you're also someone
who tricks others and steals from them.

00:18:11.758 --> 00:18:13.802
Well, this is ironic.

00:18:14.052 --> 00:18:17.889
If you ask me, you can only see
powers that can't be seen.

00:18:18.140 --> 00:18:19.600
I feel sorry for you.

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:21.184
What's that supposed to mean?

00:18:21.435 --> 00:18:26.064
I'm saying ESP isn't the only
extraordinary power people can have.

00:18:26.315 --> 00:18:27.899
Off the top of my head,

00:18:28.150 --> 00:18:31.570
I can think of four ways to defeat you.

00:18:31.820 --> 00:18:34.489
Oh? You should give them a try, then.

00:18:34.740 --> 00:18:40.329
Nah, I don't feel like it.
But I do have a request...

00:18:40.579 --> 00:18:43.040
Will you let me join you?

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:45.375
What good does that do me?

00:18:45.626 --> 00:18:48.462
I'd be able to easily persuade my
student who's unconscious there,

00:18:48.712 --> 00:18:50.631
as well as all the guys outside.

00:18:50.881 --> 00:18:53.258
That should be reason enough.

00:18:53.508 --> 00:18:56.595
Let's hear about these methods
of defeating me as well...

00:18:56.845 --> 00:18:59.264
If you actually have any, that is.

00:18:59.514 --> 00:19:03.977
I'll fill you in on some powers other
than ESP that you don't know about.

00:19:04.227 --> 00:19:05.729
The first power...

00:19:05.979 --> 00:19:09.483
The power that espers should
be extremely cautious about...

00:19:09.733 --> 00:19:10.692
That's...

00:19:10.942 --> 00:19:12.778
...brute strength, you moron!

00:19:14.279 --> 00:19:16.990
I guess I can see how you two
are master and student.

00:19:17.240 --> 00:19:19.910
What a ridiculous combination.

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:21.703
W-Wait! I give up!

00:19:21.953 --> 00:19:23.914
I'll do anything you ask.

00:19:24.164 --> 00:19:25.624
--You have put me in an extremely foul mood.

00:19:25.624 --> 00:19:26.958
--U-Um...
--You have put me in an extremely foul mood.

00:19:27.209 --> 00:19:29.378
N-N-No, wait! Let's talk about--

00:19:30.295 --> 00:19:31.254
Sto--

00:19:43.308 --> 00:19:44.976
What's going on?

00:19:45.227 --> 00:19:46.603
Reigen-san...

00:19:56.196 --> 00:19:57.364
I made it in time.

00:19:57.614 --> 00:20:01.118
I tried being courageous for once, President.

00:20:01.368 --> 00:20:04.329
Serizawa... I see that you've
completely betrayed me now.

00:20:04.579 --> 00:20:05.872
In that case...

00:20:06.123 --> 00:20:07.833
Forget it.

00:20:08.083 --> 00:20:10.210
That's enough talk.

00:20:12.754 --> 00:20:13.880
"Rage"

00:20:16.091 --> 00:20:18.635
Let me just tell you one last thing.

00:20:18.885 --> 00:20:21.638
Those who don't understand
the feelings of others...

00:20:22.681 --> 00:20:24.015
Never mind.

00:20:24.266 --> 00:20:26.893
Sometimes, you need to be
hurt to truly understand.

00:20:27.144 --> 00:20:28.311
That's...

00:20:28.562 --> 00:20:29.688
It's Nii-san.

00:20:29.938 --> 00:20:31.940
Shigeo...

00:20:32.190 --> 00:20:33.483
Mob's lost it.

00:20:33.734 --> 00:20:36.820
I-Is there anything I can help with?

00:20:37.070 --> 00:20:40.699
Serizawa-san, take my master
and the others and evacuate.

00:20:40.949 --> 00:20:42.325
Punishment comes first!

00:20:45.662 --> 00:20:46.872
Shigeo-kun!

00:20:49.791 --> 00:20:51.543
--That's...
--That's not good!

00:20:53.920 --> 00:20:54.963
Nii-san.

00:20:56.339 --> 00:20:57.549
Plants?

00:21:05.432 --> 00:21:08.769
So the boss really did cast Serizawa aside.

00:21:09.019 --> 00:21:09.978
Who?

00:21:10.228 --> 00:21:12.314
Sorry, but I owe him one.

00:21:12.564 --> 00:21:15.734
Don't, Minegishi! If you piss off the boss...

00:21:15.984 --> 00:21:18.195
So you're okay, too, Hatori.

00:21:18.445 --> 00:21:19.863
Minegishi, eh?

00:21:21.031 --> 00:21:24.367
Apparently, I'm now in a situation
where anyone can betray me.

00:21:24.618 --> 00:21:26.995
Back to the drawing board, I suppose.

00:21:27.245 --> 00:21:28.413
Disappear.

00:21:36.004 --> 00:21:39.257
Disappear. Disappear. Disappear.

00:21:44.304 --> 00:21:46.389
Well, you're enthusiastic.

00:21:46.473 --> 00:21:47.682
"Output 10%"

00:21:52.395 --> 00:21:54.731
You're weak. Too weak.

00:21:55.774 --> 00:21:58.276
I'm still only using ten percent of my powers.

00:21:58.527 --> 00:22:01.655
Is that your 100 percent?

00:22:08.161 --> 00:22:09.579
What the hell is that?

00:22:11.790 --> 00:22:15.919
I see. So that's what you were after.

00:22:16.169 --> 00:22:19.256
Now I'll be able to hit
you with everything...

00:22:19.506 --> 00:22:22.968
My powers... and my rage.

00:22:36.940 --> 00:22:42.237
I spilled a seed and lost sight of it

00:22:45.866 --> 00:22:50.745
I'll find it using the color it's dyed in
and watch it grow

00:22:53.456 --> 00:22:59.129
It immediately returned
to the palm of my hand

00:22:59.379 --> 00:23:08.471
But it's still too light and too frail
to reach for the skies

00:23:10.015 --> 00:23:14.311
The world coldly drains away all the heat

00:23:14.561 --> 00:23:18.899
The bright sunshine just isn't enough

00:23:19.149 --> 00:23:23.403
The memories are closing off what lies ahead

00:23:23.653 --> 00:23:28.825
Shake off their warmth
and set off into the distance

00:23:30.076 --> 00:23:35.332
If I let it wither, it'd be over just like that

00:23:35.582 --> 00:23:40.503
But my hope just doesn't fade away

00:23:55.894 --> 00:23:59.940
The final battle begins between an enraged
Mob and the energy demon, Suzuki.

00:24:00.190 --> 00:24:02.359
Don't push yourself too hard, Mob.

00:24:02.609 --> 00:24:04.861
Next time on Mob Psycho 100 Il Episode 13:

00:24:05.111 --> 00:24:06.780
"Boss Fight
- The Final Light~."

00:24:07.030 --> 00:24:07.238
Watching the finale in real time
is an excellent decision.

00:24:07.238 --> 00:24:09.699
"Boss Fight - The Final Light~" Watching the
finale in real time is an excellent decision.

00:24:09.699 --> 00:24:09.950
"Boss Fight
